WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.132
Once we have z scores, we can use a threshold to flag values that are far from the center of the distribution.

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:13.316
For example, values with a large absolute z score may deserve further investigation.

00:00:13.862 --> 00:00:16.969
This does not automatically mean the value is wrong.

00:00:16.969 --> 00:00:24.214
An unusual value could be a data-entry problem, or it could be a genuine and important observation.

00:00:24.214 --> 00:00:28.409
The threshold should depend on the context and distribution.

00:00:28.409 --> 00:00:34.914
The purpose of this example is to show how NumPy combines vectorized calculations, absolute values,

00:00:34.914 --> 00:00:41.115
and Boolean filtering to identify values that meet an analytical rule.
